    "vernacular": "The \"White Marble City\": since 1991 nearly every new building is faced in white marble, from ministries and hospitals to universities and apartment blocks, set along wide boulevards and manicured parks at the foot of the Kopetdag range. Landmarks are symbolic: domes and gold details, eight-pointed Oguz Khan stars, tower and globe forms. Older Soviet 1950s-80s low concrete blocks (rebuilt after the 1948 earthquake) survive in the centre. Hot dry summers, flat roofs, planted street trees and irrigated lawns.",
